# Normalize text to LF in the repository, and check it out as LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` materializes text files
# with CRLF, so `sha256sum` over the working tree does not match the SHA-256 of the
# committed content. That matters here beyond tidiness: the round-2 pre-registration
# (docs/PREREG_ribonn_part3_round2.md 7) records content hashes to prove its analysis
# code was frozen before the data was seen, and a hash that only verifies on one
# platform is not a freeze anyone can check.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets git must not touch.
*.png binary
*.gz binary
*.h5 binary
*.pth binary
*.tar.gz binary
